any other awards. The Fishermen was adapted into an award-winning ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... translated by Sinan Antoon. When Palestinians suddenly disappear, a friend of one of the vanished begins searching for clues in what John Self described as a \\\"rich, potent novel\\\".\\n\\nThis year brings a record for the longest period between an original-language publication and International Booker prize longlisting ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/feb/25/all-13-writers-on-international-booker-longlist-are-first-time-nominees\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d89\"},\"ref\":\"d89\",\"snippet\":\" ... Winner of the 2017 Man Booker International Prize.\\n\\nHerrera explores the crossings and translations people make in their minds and language as they move from one country to another, especially when there's no going back. Traversing this lonely territory is Makina, a young woman who knows only ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nypl.org/spotlight/world-literature-festival/recommended-translations\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sang Young Park (South Korea)\\n\\nPark's funny, lively, affecting novel Love in the Big City, translated by Anton Hur, was a bestseller in Korea before being longlisted for the 2022 International Booker prize. It's all about the love the narrator has experienced – for friends, for his ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/29/its-exciting-its-powerful-how-translated-fiction-captured-a-new-generation-of-readers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d91\"},\"ref\":\"d91\",\"snippet\":\" ... Prophet Song by Paul Lynch + Book Club Discussion Guide\\n\\nBooker International Prize\\n\\nA counterpart to the Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize is awarded annually for the finest single work of fiction from around the world that has been translated into English and published in the UK and ... \",\"title\":\"https://bookclubs.com/blog/2023-2024-book-awards-and-book-prize-winners\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d92\"},\"ref\":\"d92\",\"snippet\":\" ... first Indian writer to win the International Booker Prize.\\n\\nHer novel Tomb of Sand, a family saga set in the shadow of the partition of India, follows an 80-year-old woman after the death of her husband.\\n\\nIt was the first Hindi-language book to be shortlisted ... \",\"title\":\"https://literaturecurry.com/news-details/1159/geetanjali-shree-is-first-indian-to-win-inter\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... courtesy of the smallest publisher ever to win the prize, husband-and-wife indie Sort Of Books. In 2022, all the glittering literary prizes went to indies – not only the Booker, but its sister prize for translated fiction, the International Booker, as well as the Nobel, the Goldsmiths ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... Previously, the Man Booker Prize accepted work from the Commonwealth, Zimbabwe, and Ireland, but from 2014 the international Prize was widened to accept any writing in English language. An author could only win one time, and the award was valued at 60,000 British Pounds. The international award ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/the-most-prestigious-literary-awards-in-the-world.html\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"eeb1c12b9a89b0af93630999505a689f7c96e2d95575ef2c297a342405177287\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"4b79afbae42c5123f61288873423a8cd64594fb85f6f6dfb7b8138f158da2292\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize winning novels translated 25 languages\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_4a776ae543e548d88b09b766"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... winner Han Kang was eligible for this year's prize with her book We Do Not Part, translated from Korean by e. yaewon and Paige Aniyah Morris, she did not make the list. Kang won the International Booker in 2016 with her breakthrough novel, The Vegetarian, translated by ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/feb/25/all-13-writers-on-international-booker-longlist-are-first-time-nominees\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d93\"},\"ref\":\"d93\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her best known novel, The Vegetarian (published in Korea in 2007), was her first to be translated into English, in 2015. It won the Man Booker International Prize in 2016, with the prize split between Han Kang and her translator, Deborah Smith.\\n\\nAt the time, Smith's translation ... \",\"title\":\"https://theconversation.com/my-novels-explore-human-suffering-nobel-prize-winner-han-kang-writes-with-empathy-for-vulnerable-lives-241064\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d94\"},\"ref\":\"d94\",\"snippet\":\" ... the International Booker prize in 2016—The White Book, Human Acts, and Greek Lessons. Kang, 53, has been a writer for over 30 years, but The Vegetarian was her first novel to be translated into English in 2015, and led to widespread acclaim and attention.\\n\\n\\\"Han Kang writes ... \",\"title\":\"https://time.com/7065011/nobel-prize-2024-winners/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d95\"},\"ref\":\"d95\",\"snippet\":\" ... Han is the author of five books that have appeared in English: The Vegetarian (2016, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello)—which won the International Booker Prize, Human Acts (2017, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello), The White Book (2018, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello), Europa (2019, trans by Deborah ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.booksandpublishing.com.au/articles/2024/10/14/260359/han-kang-wins-2024-nobel-prize-for-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... the independent Tilted Axis Press ties in Deborah Smith, the company's founder and the translator who won the 2016 Man Booker International Prize for her translation of The Vegetarian by Korean author Han Kang\\n\\nIt's of particular importance to note that the winning International Booker Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d96\"},\"ref\":\"d96\",\"snippet\":\" ... Deborah Smith, Korean to English: 'Han Kang is very generous… she calls them \\\"our\\\" books'\\n\\nDeborah Smith is translator of The Vegetarian by the Korean writer Han Kang; she and Kang are the co-winners of the Man Booker International prize 2016. She is also the translator of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2016/jul/24/subtle-art-of-translating-foreign-fiction-ferrante-knausgaard\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d97\"},\"ref\":\"d97\",\"snippet\":\" ... International Booker Prize\\n\\nFocusing on contemporary fiction originally written in English and published outside the UK and Ireland, this award champions exceptional storytelling from around the globe. Previous winners include Marlon James for \\\"A Brief History of Seven Killings\\\" and Han Kang for \\\"The Vegetarian,\\\" showcasing new and ... \",\"title\":\"https://inkerspress.com/top-10-most-prestigious-international-literary-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... of the 2m books of translated fiction sold in Britain last year, she tells me, \\\"the single most popular language – just under half a million volumes – was Japanese\\\" (not including manga), \\\"followed by South Korean\\\". (Anton Hur, a Booker-longlisted translator, recently wrote that after The Vegetarian won ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/29/its-exciting-its-powerful-how-translated-fiction-captured-a-new-generation-of-readers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d98\"},\"ref\":\"d98\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Accusation, which was written in secret and smuggled out of the country, is his only published book to date. Deborah Smith is the Man Booker International Prize–winning translator of The Vegetarian by Han Kang and other books.\\n\\nHarmless Like You by Rowan Hisayo Buchanan\\n\\nRowan Hisayo ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d99\"},\"ref\":\"d99\",\"snippet\":\" ... And for those of us interested in reading books that originate beyond the English-speaking world, they don't come much more major than the Man Booker International Prize, which was awarded for the first time last year to Han Kang and translator Deborah Smith for The Vegetarian ... \",\"title\":\"https://ayearofreadingtheworld.com/2017/04/29/book-of-the-month-samanta-schweblin/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"7d995f7b7b42a5a635a0cafed0ed5dddddafc2dc8ac5e4d634232c9e4ac5e341\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"5ae117f2314097606886b1c6760e92473dd1076e37fc74ed0ede7fc2110b1555\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Vegetarian Han Kang translated languages International Booker\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d100\"},\"ref\":\"d100\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2018, \\\"Flights\\\" won the International Booker Prize, Britain's most important recognition for literature in translation, with the prize's chair, Lisa Appignanesi, heralding Tokarczuk as \\\"a writer of wonderful wit, imagination, and literary panache.\\\" Thanks to the Booker win, the author already had an eager readership ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2024/07/08/fitzcarraldo-editions-makes-challenging-literature-chic\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... the most significant young publishers of translated fiction is Jacques Testard's Fitzcarraldo Editions, which since its inception in 2014 has published one International Booker prize winner (Olga Tokarczuk's Flights, translated by Jennifer Croft) and three Nobel literature laureates: Tokarczuk, Annie Ernaux and Svetlana Alexievich.\\n\\nSo what ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/29/its-exciting-its-powerful-how-translated-fiction-captured-a-new-generation-of-readers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2018, the Polish novelist was recognized for \\\"Flights,\\\" which she calls a \\\"constellation novel,\\\" owing to its fragmentary form and genre-defying style, and which won that year's Man Booker Prize. \\\"Drive Your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead,\\\" her latest novel to be translated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... In London, Geetanjali Shree and Daisy Rockwell Win the 2022 International Booker Prize\\nauthor: Porter Anderson\\ndate: 2022-05-26\\n---\\n'Tomb of Sand' is the first novel translated from an Indian language to win the award. Shree and Rockwell split the International Booker's £50,000 purse.\\n\\nBy ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d97\"},\"ref\":\"d97\",\"snippet\":\" ... Man Booker International Prize\\n\\nCelebrating the best-translated fiction, this biennial award recognizes a single book translated into English and published in the UK or Ireland. From Salman Rushdie's \\\"Midnight's Children\\\" to Olga Tokarczuk's \\\"Flights,\\\" it champions diverse voices and fosters global literary exchange!\\n\\nPremio ... \",\"title\":\"https://inkerspress.com/top-10-most-prestigious-international-literary-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d101\"},\"ref\":\"d101\",\"snippet\":\" ... Nobel Prize in Literature for 2018 in December 2019, becoming the fifth Polish-language laureate. For decades, she has been the best-selling author in Poland. Tokarczuk gained international popularity after becoming the first Polish author to win the Man Booker International Award in 2018 for Flights (Bieguni ... \",\"title\":\"https://researchinpoland.org/polish-nobel-prize-winners/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d102\"},\"ref\":\"d102\",\"snippet\":\" ... Olga Tokarczuk was a Finalist for Translated Literature in 2018 and Longlisted in 2019. The authors and translators on the list have been recognized by numerous international prizes, including the Akutagawa Prize, the Prix de la Littérature Arabe, the International Booker Prize, and the PEN Translation Prize. Their ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nationalbook.org/2022-national-book-awards-longlist-for-translated-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d103\"},\"ref\":\"d103\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book was later translated by Antonia Lloyd Jones and published in 2019 by Riverhead Books, earning nominations to 2019 Man Booker International Prize (short list) and Warwick Prize for Women in Translation (short list) and .\\n\\nThe short story is probably your favorite literary form, which you care ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bklynlibrary.org/blog/2020/01/12/olga-tokarczuk-interview\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2022, all the glittering literary prizes went to indies – not only the Booker, but its sister prize for translated fiction, the International Booker, as well as the Nobel, the Goldsmiths, the Pulitzer and Australia's A$100,000 (£80,000) Victorian prize for literature. The last four ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d104\"},\"ref\":\"d104\",\"snippet\":\" ... Jennifer Croft won a 2022 Guggenheim Fellowship for her novel The Extinction of Irena Rey, the 2020 William Saroyan International Prize for Writing for her illustrated memoir Homesick, and the 2018 International Booker Prize for her translation of Olga Tokarczuk's Flights. A two-time National Book Award ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nationalbook.org/2024-national-book-awards-judges/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"79c684a3c306801c606722e697d5f144b4a4b91e1d5a8da9d6feecb3c0f92d9a\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"ded9d5bd41864429aecef96c693d5061358da8277a9eb669dcb81a35a2ac302b\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Flights Tokarczuk translated languages International Booker Prize\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d105\"},\"ref\":\"d105\",\"snippet\":\" ... Celestial Bodies: A Novel, Jokha Alharthi (Oct. 15)\\n\\nThree Omani sisters grapple with love and loss as their country quickly transforms due to the rise of the oil industry. Celestial Bodies, the first novel originally published in Arabic to win the Man Booker International Prize, showcases Oman's ... \",\"title\":\"https://time.com/5661400/best-books-fall-2019/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d106\"},\"ref\":\"d106\",\"snippet\":\" ... Unsurprisingly, these will come from authors whose works have already won awards in translation: Jokha al-Harthi (winner of the Man Booker International) and Khaled Khalifa (twice shortlisted for the National Book Award). Both have been Englished by their award-winning translators, Marilyn Booth and Leri Price.\\n\\nWhile ... \",\"title\":\"https://arablit.org/2021/11/30/forthcoming-2022-arabic-literature-in-english-translation/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d107\"},\"ref\":\"d107\",\"snippet\":\" ... by Margaret Mitsutani\\n\\n(New Directions)\\n\\n9 Rave • 6 Positive • 1 Mixed\\n\\n\\\"… mordantly funny … More than simply international, her writing is translingual; she leaves the borders between languages open and allows them to cross-pollinate. To translate her into English is to excavate linguistic strata: Panska reads like a ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-best-reviewed-literature-in-translation-of-2022/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d108\"},\"ref\":\"d108\",\"snippet\":\" ... What if the resolution is the start of a new nightmare? Jones unspools just how nebulous the traumas of a single wrongful conviction can be for everyone involved; she moves between the perspectives of Roy, Celestial, and their friend Andre, whose connection with Celestial deepens into something fierce ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theatlantic.com/entertainment/archive/2018/12/the-19-best-books-2018/578134/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d109\"},\"ref\":\"d109\",\"snippet\":\" ... McGee\\n\\nTranslated from the English by Izak de Vries\\n\\nCatalyst Press | 2023\\n\\nThis Afrikaans-language children's book, also published in English by Catalyst Press, takes readers \\\"on an adventure through human history to find out why skin is the hardest working organ in the body business.\\\"\\n\\nJohn ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.clmp.org/news/a-reading-list-for-national-translation-month-2024/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d110\"},\"ref\":\"d110\",\"snippet\":\" ... My Sor Juana by July Westhale\\n\\nSmall Harbor Publishing | 2024\\n\\nIn this poetry collection, \\\"Westhale's translations and marginal notes on Sor Juana Inés de la Cruz's sonnets conjure a brilliant dialogue across desires, languages, and centuries.\\\"\\n\\nSubsisters: Selected Poems by Uljana Wolf\\n\\nTranslated from the German ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.clmp.org/news/a-reading-list-for-women-in-translation-month-2024/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... Related awards for translated works\\n\\nA separate prize for which any living writer in the world may qualify, the Man Booker International Prize, was inaugurated in 2005. Until 2015, it was given every two years to a living author of any nationality for a body of work published ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d48\"},\"ref\":\"d48\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d89\"},\"ref\":\"d89\",\"snippet\":\" ... Winner of the 2017 Man Booker International Prize.\\n\\nHerrera explores the crossings and translations people make in their minds and language as they move from one country to another, especially when there's no going back. Traversing this lonely territory is Makina, a young woman who knows only ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nypl.org/spotlight/world-literature-festival/recommended-translations\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previo